    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Chadwick (1932) replaced the proton-electron nucleus with the modern picture: a nucleus of mass number A and atomic number Z is exactly Z protons and N=A-Z neutrons. Three years later, Weizsacker combined this proton-neutron picture with a liquid-drop model into a single closed-form estimate of nuclear binding energy,">

